2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ in the numerator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253630 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02f785b1-458a-5fb7-aba5-77cefec577f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250579} {:answer/id #uuid "49bb700e-a1de-516d-87ba-f936ef57ceae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251166} {:answer/id #uuid "6a8f3721-64a5-5d00-9f26-2a8bc5dfc279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218