2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253634 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a688a79-b89b-5a35-859e-9149fddd7243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250780} {:answer/id #uuid "707de248-a804-5090-bb48-1024b7978c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251472} {:answer/id #uuid "88d27f46-cee8-5aaf-a22c-9714e10049d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251708} {:answer/id #uuid "8d7b26e1-8cd7-5f50-a6e4-a5249bb1359c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251750} {:answer/id #uuid "cb2cbc2a-146e-503b-a70d-071b522d1db3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a688a79-b89b-5a35-859e-9149fddd7243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250780} :answer-field/id #uuid "245bab01-767a-51fa-a844-da9fd9dcf4a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a04b487-4a85-5ba7-af3b-ed0dfdddcb78" :question/math-academy-id "q-120032" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={105}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}) & =4(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡{210}^{∘} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})=-2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253636 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12fcc529-6327-5a47-a71b-9884c98ea937" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250715} {:answer/id #uuid "452da317-cd5b-5e2c-a807-a5fb3eafe527" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251127} {:answer/id #uuid "61086b08-503f-5afe-8d5f-93b7e8662a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251347} {:answer/id #uuid "b2646330-ca77-5a0d-b193-c06bcdc7a115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252111} {:answer/id #uuid "d26cc6ac-3efb-5846-8c19-760d22ea431d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61086b08-503f-5afe-8d5f-93b7e8662a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251347} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f04de3e-9c49-5ec2-bb16-a4b47af64121" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ad1365bd-d309-5764-8412-78c271945c47" :question/math-academy-id "q-120058" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253643 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04698c75-dc83-5fbb-8f53-9052909b1e30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250585} {:answer/id #uuid "1b2c3035-0235-5603-a72a-eb385d8843e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250786} {:answer/id #uuid "6012bda1-9035-5aff-82de-2b534c046c57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251340} {:answer/id #uuid "9aad87db-038e-549a-b557-3d3499e0f30c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251882} {:answer/id #uuid "df46eab3-2fa6-5ef3-9539-002572011a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6012bda1-9035-5aff-82de-2b534c046c57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251340} :answer-field/id #uuid "e90d146b-981f-56ed-88e6-d9ffffc3ab01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253212}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "91b3ae38-a411-55e5-ba0c-b0976c1d82dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-120093" :question/problem "$8\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{32}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{32})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}).\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}) & =4[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{16},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}) & =2[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})] \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{16})] \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253660 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ee252b3-2fc9-58a1-a526-0ad834b9b6a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3(2x-3)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250686} {:answer/id #uuid "18391112-3f3a-57a1-9bfe-ef48a937491a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{(2x-3)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250766} {:answer/id #uuid "1e9cae62-9c68-5e87-9549-65a72091d03a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{(2x-3)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250813} {:answer/id #uuid "405c4f12-0925-5899-8b0c-bf237460ec93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3(2x-3)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251088} {:answer/id #uuid "988c1baf-6f97-581c-b7f2-f8c57f43988e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{(2x-3)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "988c1baf-6f97-581c-b7f2-f8c57f43988e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{(2x-3)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251863} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae027c21-9aa0-573c-bcf0-1d5cd80234b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "03a455ba-2873-5368-831e-308d6a1a251d" :question/math-academy-id "q-12018" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{6}{(2x-3)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 6(2x-3)^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2x-3.$Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6(2x-3)^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6{u}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int {u}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3}){u}^{-3}+C \\\\  & =-{u}^{-3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(2x-3)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{(2x-3)^{3}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{(2x-3)^{3}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(2x-3)^{-3}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-(-3)\\cdot (2x-3)^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-3)+0 \\\\  & =3\\cdot (2x-3)^{-4}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(2x-3)^{4}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c6f4f87-1ccd-589c-90e1-8890c55c15eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,\\frac{7\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250932} {:answer/id #uuid "62a869bc-7ad8-5514-a78a-02dff1b40c81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,\\frac{5\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251359} {:answer/id #uuid "89286d84-c732-59b4-956d-104585bfdb9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251711} {:answer/id #uuid "94083696-43f4-54f2-b3f6-a3866a469f41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251825} {:answer/id #uuid "a5579b86-e0b3-519e-954e-6b1008604303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,\\frac{3\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5579b86-e0b3-519e-954e-6b1008604303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,\\frac{3\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251978} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd003bc0-32be-5a18-932b-9a7f1e93dea2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0eb4fa3e-52f2-52cc-a5b3-7f2b007d645a" :question/math-academy-id "q-120234" :question/problem "A point $P$ has Cartesian coordinates $(-\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{2}).$ What are the polar coordinates of $P?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we determine $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{2})^{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2+2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the reference angle, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & =|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{-\\sqrt{2}})| \\\\  & =|-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)| \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the point $P$ lies in the second quadrant, we subtract the reference angle from $\\pi ,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar coordinates of $P$ are  $(2,\\frac{3\\pi }{4}).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253668 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "049efc1d-4c7f-52f6-9cd8-9ae1c6f88cf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{2}\\text{ }\\,a,3.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250588} {:answer/id #uuid "66d1cb3d-aadc-5b70-9414-a02961598fff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5\\text{ }\\,a,2.6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251397} {:answer/id #uuid "ca9dbdde-773a-5fb9-9921-474c631d48f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{5}\\text{ }\\,a,2.7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252348} {:answer/id #uuid "cd82bd9e-d87e-5ee9-b28f-3cdf48082798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\text{ }\\,a,2.8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252365} {:answer/id #uuid "d23227b1-bcd0-53d7-b1ec-28eb92816360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{5}\\text{ }\\,a,4.6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca9dbdde-773a-5fb9-9921-474c631d48f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{5}\\text{ }\\,a,2.7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252348} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6ee89f8-248f-5891-989b-af26eedc236e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253121}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0c3da906-9678-5457-978c-c32d8842e209" :question/math-academy-id "q-120241" :question/problem "A point $P$ has Cartesian coordinates $(-2a,a),$ where $a$ is a positive real number. What are the polar coordinates of $P?$  Round your answer to the nearest tenth where appropriate." :question/worked-solution "First, we determine $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2a)^{2}+{a}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{a}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\text{ }\\,a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the reference angle, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & =|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{-2a})| \\\\  & =|-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})| \\\\  & ≈0.463\\,6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the point $P$ lies in the second quadrant, we subtract the reference angle from $\\pi ,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ≈\\pi -0.463\\,6 \\\\  & ≈2.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar coordinates of $P$ are  $(\\sqrt{5}\\text{ }\\,a,2.7).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253669 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "191782ef-158c-5c61-8b5a-53889b26df66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{2}\\text{ }\\,a,\\frac{7\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250772} {:answer/id #uuid "27773dbc-82c6-5d97-8262-5945a24bc201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\text{ }\\,a,\\frac{5\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250891} {:answer/id #uuid "4683b3fe-eb8e-5220-9fa6-0a9afcd7c7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{2}\\tex