ore, the polar coordinates of $P$ are  $(\\sqrt{2}\\text{ }\\,a,\\frac{3\\pi }{4}).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256387 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2075c86f-b918-575b-95e8-97859e70f90d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253951} {:answer/id #uuid "52496fb6-06f9-54e1-953b-c03cfcd9334c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2\\sqrt{2},-2\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254387} {:answer/id #uuid "6724825c-031e-5303-abbe-a1eba30f6cba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254603} {:answer/id #uuid "8470b6c3-3213-5f69-8af6-c90604195120" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\sqrt{2},-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254848} {:answer/id #uuid "b04df24b-bdd0-5a86-9ea8-ddd583bd9c28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\sqrt{2},-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52496fb6-06f9-54e1-953b-c03cfcd9334c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2\\sqrt{2},-2\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254387} :answer-field/id #uuid "5736a212-726e-5d37-950e-cb5984448244" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cffd31fb-6e24-58d9-bedb-a4c483fcb431" :question/math-academy-id "q-120311" :question/problem "The point $P$ has polar coordinates $(4,{225}^{∘}).$ Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P.$" :question/worked-solution "To convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡({225}^{∘}) \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({225}^{∘}) \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(-2\\sqrt{2},-2\\sqrt{2}).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256389 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48fc86a1-f2ca-5fb6-98bb-2ba50587b6e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3\\sqrt{2},-3\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254297} {:answer/id #uuid "6e2e5dea-eb32-5ef7-b053-292457b74c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254647} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e86342-c856-59b9-acc7-8c16b2779f05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\sqrt{3},-2\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255156} {:answer/id #uuid "bceb10bc-923e-5dff-8dfb-386a60cdb562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6\\sqrt{2},6\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255360} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3e4f69-01dd-5d42-b6e1-f9b19a563b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3},-\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48fc86a1-f2ca-5fb6-98bb-2ba50587b6e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3\\sqrt{2},-3\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254297} :answer-field/id #uuid "af20ccec-9741-587e-8b2c-0fb701159ee6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3fe83e25-a491-5f7c-b624-e2aecbbcfc65" :question/math-academy-id "q-120328" :question/problem "Given that the distance from a point $P$ to the origin is $6,$ and that $P$ makes an angle of ${315}^{∘}$ with the positive $x$-axis, what are the Cartesian coordinates of $P?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that the point $P$ is described using polar coordinates $(r,\\theta )$, where\n\n$$\nr=6,\\,\\theta ={315}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTo convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡({315}^{∘}) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{sin}⁡({315}^{∘}) \\\\  & =6(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(3\\sqrt{2},-3\\sqrt{2}).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256392 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61d023a1-2aa7-5888-bcf0-be644edf4473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254547} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2ff8db-4995-5531-9ef6-10f0585e85d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254923} {:answer/id #uuid "96f239ff-4f7d-598d-ae07-5b24ea0f2611" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/